Verdict: PASS. I wrote it to session_plan/eval_task_2.md. The REPL path is covered only by unit tests on the new helper; nobody, including me, has seen it work in a live REPL session.

• REPL: before each user turn, the REPL now clears the checkpoint flag (CHECKPOINT_TRIGGERED). The auto-continue loop then goes through a small new function, auto_continue_allowed. When a checkpoint stop blocks a continue, it prints one dim line saying auto-continue was skipped and why.
• Clearing the flag is safe: I searched for every reader of CHECKPOINT_TRIGGERED. Only the -p and piped exit-code paths read it (main.rs:708 and :1050); the REPL never does, so clearing it per turn can't change an exit code.
• Piped mode: piped_should_continue now refuses to continue after a checkpoint stop when --continue-on-silence is on. Its call site in main.rs:965 and all the existing test calls in main_tests.rs were updated for the extra argument.
• Tests: one of the new tests takes a real checkpoint-stopped run and first shows that, without the fix, auto-continue would have continued it. The tests that the stop blocks it are therefore checking something real.
• Unused definitions: none. Both new definitions (auto_continue_allowed and the skip message constant) are used in this diff. The repl.rs line-count limit in tests/module_size.rs was raised to 3411, with a reason.
• Docs: updated in docs/src/features/context.md and docs/src/usage/repl.md.
• Product safety: behaviour only changes for users who chose --context-strategy checkpoint. No defaults or flags changed.
